  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I noticed a new trend in UI updates: Now a lot of long texts being placed into short-living pop-ups/alerts/notifications.\n\nInstead of simply saying \"Instance full\" or something similar it puts miles long wall of text into notification that end user should read and understand in a second.\n\nThose messages are not user friendly at all: they should be either\n\n- be dismissible\n\n- live much longer\n\n- text must be simplified\n\nPeople simply can't understand lots of text that fast.\n\nPlease note, I am not talking about broken text layouts here.",
